  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      58.32,
      477.55,
      525.76,
      546.19
    ],
    "text": "The depression located over the northwest Bay of Bengal, northeast of the island, is expected to further intensify into a deep depression within the next 12 hours. Although this system will not have a direct impact on Sri Lanka, the prevailing rainy conditions in the southwestern part of the island are expected to continue due to the wind flow towards the system.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold",
      "Iskoola Pota,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      0.9599999785423279,
      2.0399999618530273,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      58.32,
      549.88,
      534.05,
      606.58
    ],
    "text": "Showers or thundershowers will occur at times in the Western, Sabaragamuwa, Central and North-western provinces and in Galle and Matara Districts. Heavy falls above 100 mm are likely at some places in the above areas.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      6.960000038146973,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      58.32,
      609.49,
      463.73,
      627.58
    ],
    "text": "Several spells of showers may occur in North-central province and Mannar district.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      3.0,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      58.32,
      636.13,
      533.94,
      766.05
    ],
    "text": "Strong winds of about (40-50) kmph can be expected at times over Western slopes of the Central hills, North-central and North-western provinces and in Trincomalee, Hambantota and Matale Districts. The general public is kindly requested to take adequate precautions to minimize damage caused by temporary localized strong winds and lightning during thundershowers.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      3.0,
